<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n36343" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pindărus</span></b> , i,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Πίνδαρος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Pindar</i>, <i>a celebrated lyric poet
				of Thebes</i>, <i>contemporary with
				Æschylus</i>, <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 4,
				2, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Quint. 10, 1, 61</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. Fin.
				2, 34, 115</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sen.
				Q. N. 6, 26, 3</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pindărĕ-us</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Pindaric</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pindaream chelyn referre,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 2, § 119</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pin-dărĭcus</span></b> , a, um,
				adj., <i>Pindaric</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Camenae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 9, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ep. 1, 3, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Pindaricos modos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					8, 18, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ov. P. 4, 16, 28</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">os,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prop. 3, 15, 40</span></i>
			: Pindaricum metrum, consisting of a trimeter
				brachycatalectus
			 (e. g. medium rapido mare Tibris adit fluvio),
					<i><span class="en">Serv. Centimetr. p. 1822</span></i>
			P.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Name of a slave</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Att.
				16, 1, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Inscr. Murat. 619,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>The freedman who held the sword upon which Cassius
				fell at Philippi</i>, <i><span class="en">Val. Max. 6, 8, 4</span></i>.</div>
